Again, ?  I've never had a problem doing damage with a barbarian; the
original battle axe serves perfectly well until you trip over or wish up
whatever your preferred toy is this week; again, not that it matters
since Barbs can ascend with a wielded chest.  (Also, don't forget to factor 
the effort and turns required to obtain Cleaver into all this (fickle
gods are a nuisance)).

As far as time... I'm not referring to the time spent actually doing the 
alchemy, but the time and effort required to lug around (and keep safe) 
all those damn potions.  When you're not worried about preserving all the 
different types necessary for alchemy (speed and gain ability/gain level), it
makes it a lot easier to ID potions on the fly.

For that matter, I'd seriously consider leaving all non-full-healing potions
behind or quaffing them on-the-spot to prevent monsters from using them.
They don't heal anywhere near what I'll want, and Barbs may start with
high STR/CON but offloading any bit of crap helps.

